--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/places.json
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Derived from the GeoNames geographical database (cities500 dump).

  Source:  https://download.geonames.org/export/dump/
  Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0)
           https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Credit:  "This product includes data created by GeoNames (www.geonames.org),
           licensed under CC BY 4.0."

The file is a filtered extract, not the dump: US and Canadian populated places
(GeoNames feature codes PPL, PPLA*, PPLC, PPLG) within roughly 55 km of ocean
coastline or a major lake, carrying name, region, position and population only.
`scripts/build-places.mjs` regenerates it and records the exact filter.

Natural Earth 1:10m coastline and lakes are used by that script as a spatial
filter. Natural Earth is public domain, and no Natural Earth geometry appears in
the output.

Redistributing this file downstream carries the CC BY attribution requirement
with it. The rest of the package — corrections, registry, gazetteer, code — is
our own work under MIT, and PROVENANCE.md documents where those facts come from.
